hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16018","Abu al-Walid Hisham narrated to us, he said, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik, from Ibn Abi al-Mualla, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave a sermon one day and said: A man was given choice by his Lord, mighty and majestic, between living in this world as long as he wishes to live in it, eating of this world as much as he wishes to eat of it, and between meeting his Lord, mighty and majestic, and he chose meeting his Lord. He said, so Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, wept. He said, so the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you not marvel at this old man, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned a righteous man whom his Lord, blessed and exalted, gave choice between this world and between meeting his Lord, blessed and exalted, and he chose meeting his Lord, mighty and majestic, and Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, was the most knowledgeable of them of what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, and Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Rather we ransom you with our wealth and our children, or with our fathers. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is none of the people more generous to us in his companionship and his wealth than Ibn Abi Quhafah, and had I taken an intimate friend, I would have taken Ibn Abi Quhafah, but affection and brotherhood of faith, but affection and brotherhood of faith, twice, and your companion is the intimate friend of Allah, mighty and majestic."
